  <div class="honest-take">
    <p class="honest-take__label">Honest take</p>
    <p>
      SEO is easier to self-verify: you either found the broken canonical tag and fixed it, or you did
      not, and Search Console tells you which. Content marketing is harder to self-verify because voice
      and editorial judgment take longer to develop and are harder to grade against a checklist — a
      technically "correct" article can still be forgettable. Neither of these makes one field "easier."
      It changes what kind of practice environment and timeline you honestly need before you can call
      yourself job-ready.
    </p>
